    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and the duplicate-detection behavior as specified.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 rewrote `key(telephone, email, lastName)` to return the full lower-case hex **SHA-256** of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (a 64-char hex string). The third argument changed from `householdId` to `lastName`. Added a standard American **`soundex()`** helper (first letter + three zero-padded digits, collapsing adjacent same-digit letters, vowels resetting the run, `h`/`w` transparent). `householdId()`/`customerHash()` are untouched since other steps still use them.\n\n**`RequireUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 409 detection now keys purely off the single `identityKey` computed from `lastName` (no longer folding in the computed `householdId`, so that separate household-duplicate block is gone). Still skips owners flagged `deleted`, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (`requireEmailDomain` precedes this step in `owners.POST.yml`).\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 soft match now triggers when the new owner's `identityKey` **differs** from an existing owner's but their `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match. Because telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they're created and flagged as a soft match against the earliest-created match. Declared household members (`sharesHousehold`) and deleted owners are still excluded.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `identityKey` DTO mapping now passes `owner.getLastName()` instead of `owner.getHouseholdId()`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `possibleDuplicateOf` descriptions/example to reflect the SHA-256/soundex design.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the collision \u2192 409) both pass.",
